  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}$ are non-coplanar vectors and $\\lambda$ is a real number then $\\left[\\lambda(\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}) \\lambda^2 \\vec{b} \\lambda \\vec{c}\\right]=[\\vec{a} \\vec{b}+\\vec{c} \\vec{b}]$ for"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\nexactly one value of $\\lambda$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nno value of $\\lambda$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\nexactly three values of $\\lambda$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nexactly two values of $\\lambda$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& {\\left[\\begin{array}{lll}\n\\lambda(\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}) & \\lambda^2 \\vec{b} & \\lambda \\vec{c}\n\\end{array}\\right]=\\left[\\begin{array}{lll}\n\\vec{a} & \\vec{b}+\\vec{c} & \\vec{b}\n\\end{array}\\right]} \\\\\n& \\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n\\lambda & \\lambda & 0 \\\\\n0 & \\lambda^2 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 0 & \\lambda\n\\end{array}\\right|=\\left|\\begin{array}{lll}\n1 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 1 & 1 \\\\\n0 & 1 & 0\n\\end{array}\\right| \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\lambda^4=-1 \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nHence no real value of $\\lambda$."
  }
}